    "q-184529": {
      "dom_id": "step-q184529",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[i,1]\\times \\{i\\}.$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[0.5,1]\\times \\{0.5\\}=\\{(k,0.5)\\,:\\,k\\in [0.5,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a horizontal line segment from the point $(0.5,0.5)$ to the point $(1,0.5)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14249122/assets/bb8f515fb5c342ece5727830e95bcc617c03a5bf6542f959ba9e020d22f7faef.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[i,1]\\times \\{i\\}=\\{(k,i)\\,:\\,k\\in [i,1]\\}\n$$\n\nis the horizontal line segment from the point $(i,i)$ to the point $(1,i).$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14249122/assets/f255d7dede080e93cb135c1087a0f14591467439d891187062a4fa185a8858cf.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following triangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14249122/assets/d823dd4dcd675b07b004cf2850059600e861c8b3d259f884d25c61e43431de35.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
